{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01NQv687MMhCjDhGwKTEM34L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MrfiGHVkGMvLkExWQg5WRx","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a top ML venue review. Your focus: **Methods and Experiments**. Evaluate rigor, soundness, ablation completeness, statistical validity, and reproducibility.\n\nUse a 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept. Target venue acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nTitle: \"Episode-Level Credit Assignment for Multi-Turn Agent Training: Learning When to Verify via Reinforcement Learning\"\n\nThe paper makes two contributions:\n1. **Episode-level GRPO** resolves credit assignment collapse in multi-turn agent RL. Step-independent training achieves 0% on ALFWorld; episode-level achieves 34.9±4.7%. Validated via h-sweep (h∈{2,5,10,20,full}), ScienceWorld transfer (22.8% vs 3.1%), and 7B scaling (48.4% vs 5.3%).\n2. **B-IAVR** (selective verification): trains binary verify/skip policy using action-change reward. Reduces verification cost by 22% with 4.6pp success trade-off. Marginally outperforms random-50%, roughly matches confidence-threshold baseline.\n\n## Key Experimental Results to Evaluate\n\n**Table 1 (Core result):** Episode-level mean 34.9±4.7% (3 seeds: 35.9/29.7/39.1) vs step-independent 0%.\n\n**Table 2 (h-sweep):** h=2→0%, h=5→4.7%, h=10→18.8%, h=20→29.7%, full→35.9%. Some noise between h=10 and h=20 across seeds.\n\n**Table 3 (Gradient analysis):** Gradient variance 0.89 at h=2, 0.12 at full. Relative gradient signal tracks effective discount.\n\n**Table 4 (Per-task):** Success correlates with episode length (r=-0.87). pick=42.1%, pick_two=18.2%.\n\n**Table 5 (Generalization):** ScienceWorld 22.8% vs 3.1%. Qwen3-7B: 48.4% vs 5.3%.\n\n**Table 6 (Verification value):** Always-on 35.9% vs no-verify 23.4% (12.5pp gap).\n\n**Tables 7-8 (Action-change):** 68.8% confirmatory. Correlation r=0.19 (p=0.003). Partial correlation after entropy control r=0.14 (p=0.031).\n\n**Table 9 (Causal intervention):** Verification-triggered 39.2% vs random 31.8% vs no-change 34.1%. p=0.042.\n\n**Table 10 (B-IAVR training):** Converges to 31.3% success, 71.2% verify rate at step 18.\n\n**Table 11 (Full comparison):** B-IAVR 31.3%/71.2% vs confidence-threshold 30.5%/62.4% vs random-50% 28.1%/50% vs no-verify 23.4%.\n\n**Table 12 (Reward ablation):** Action-change 31.3%/22.1% cost reduction vs confidence-based 30.1%/24.8% vs random 27.8%/31.4%.\n\n**Table 13 (ARES comparison):** B-IAVR 31.3%/22.1% cost reduction vs ARES 29.7%/33.8%.\n\n## Review Context (Imagined Experiment Coverage)\n\nThe review_context.yaml lists 15 planned experiments. The paper covers all of them. Key concerns from context:\n- h-sweep has noise (not perfectly monotonic across seeds)\n- Multi-seed std=4.7pp (moderate variance)\n- Action-change correlation weak (r=0.19 raw, r=0.14 partial)\n- B-IAVR selective verification effect not dramatic (only 22% cost reduction, 4.6pp success loss)\n- B-IAVR barely beats confidence-threshold (+0.8pp)\n- ARES comparison is mixed (ARES gets better cost reduction)\n- Causal intervention p=0.042 barely significant\n\n## Your Task\n\nWrite a detailed review covering:\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (bulleted, specific)\n3. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, specific, with severity: minor/moderate/major)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (3-5 specific questions)\n5. **Missing Experiments / Analysis**\n6. **Scores**: Soundness (1-4), Contribution (1-4), Clarity (1-4), Overall (1-6), Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous but fair. Focus on methodological soundness and experimental design.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33736,"cache_read_input_tokens":24215,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33736},"output_tokens":18,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10a3f31b-71c7-4a9c-9f06-cb705222db6e","uuid":"e37b1b4b-fc2d-4caf-9829-fbd60dd3efbf"}
