{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014YZHjSxD3JEcHcwf2fqBic","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is a summary of the R2 assessment:\n\n**Overall: 3/6 (Weak Reject)**\n\nKey findings:\n\n1. **Episode-level GRPO has low novelty.** It is functionally equivalent to REINFORCE (1992) with trajectory returns. The gamma^(T-h) \"discovery\" is a mathematical tautology. The paper frames a one-line configuration fix as a methodological contribution.\n\n2. **B-IAVR results are marginal.** Actual improvements over confidence-threshold are +0.8pp (within seed noise). Even the dream paper's +2.5pp is not statistically distinguishable from zero given std=2.9pp.\n\n3. **Related work is critically inadequate.** 10 references in 3 paragraphs. Missing entire categories: classic RL credit assignment (GAE, RUDDER), concurrent agent RL (GiGPO at 86.1%, HCAPO, PA-MoE at 93.8%), selective verification competitors (Derailer-Rerailer, Agent-Omit, Sherlock), and the self-correction literature.\n\n4. **Absolute performance far below SOTA.** The paper achieves 34.9-48.2% on ALFWorld while Self-Guide gets 72.7% (same model) and PA-MoE+GiGPO gets 93.8% (smaller model). The \"8x improvement\" framing compares against a known-broken baseline, which is circular.\n\n5. **False dichotomy in credit assignment.** The paper presents only step-independent vs. episode-level, ignoring the rich intermediate spectrum (GiGPO nested groups, GAE, hindsight credit) that achieves higher performance.\n\nThe review was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T235255/best/review_report.md`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ae19fc4ca933e3405 (use SendMessage with to: 'ae19fc4ca933e3405' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 56335\ntool_uses: 15\nduration_ms: 134731</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"10a3f31b-71c7-4a9c-9f06-cb705222db6e","uuid":"22f758cb-1af8-4b0f-b512-196b3576852e","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:24:05.729Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) for a top ML venue review. Your focus: **Novelty and Related Work**. Evaluate originality, positioning relative to prior art, whether the contribution is sufficient for a top venue, and framing/writing quality.\n\nUse a 6-point scale: 1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept. Target venue acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nTitle: \"Episode-Level Credit Assignment for Multi-Turn Agent Training: Learning When to Verify via Reinforcement Learning\"\n\nThe paper makes two contributions:\n1. **Episode-level GRPO** resolves credit assignment collapse in multi-turn agent RL. Step-independent training achieves 0% on ALFWorld; episode-level achieves 34.9±4.7%. The credit assignment failure is characterized via h-sweep (h∈{2,5,10,20,full}), gradient signal analysis, ScienceWorld transfer, and 7B scaling.\n2. **B-IAVR** (Binary Informativeness-Aware Verification by RL): trains a selective verification policy using action-change as intrinsic reward. Reduces verification cost by 22% with 4.6pp success trade-off. Marginally outperforms random-50%, roughly matches confidence-threshold baseline.\n\n## Method Details\n\n- Episode-level GRPO: attributes episode reward R equally to all steps. Policy gradient uses batch-normalized rewards. Eliminates discount-based decay.\n- B-IAVR reward: R = R_task + α·Σ(action_changed when verified) - β·Σ(verify count). α=0.5, β=0.1.\n- Base model: Qwen3-1.7B. Environments: ALFWorld (primary), ScienceWorld (transfer). Also tested Qwen3-7B.\n\n## Related Work as Written in Paper\n\nThree paragraphs:\n1. **RL for LM Agents**: RAGEN, AgentTrek, WebRL. Claims these systems assume per-step credit assignment is sufficient.\n2. **Self-Verification and Reflection**: Self-Guide (72.7% on ALFWorld with Qwen-1.7B, always-on), ReflAct (GPT-4), Inner Monologue.\n3. **Adaptive Computation and Selective Reasoning**: ARES (SFT router, 52.7% token reduction), Thinkless (RL for reasoning tokens, single-turn).\n\nOnly 10 references total.\n\n## Key Results for Novelty Assessment\n\n- Episode-level vs step-independent: 34.9% vs 0% (dramatic gap)\n- B-IAVR vs confidence-threshold: 31.3% vs 30.5% (marginal, +0.8pp)\n- B-IAVR vs ARES: 31.3%/22.1% cost reduction vs 29.7%/33.8% (mixed, neither dominates)\n- Action-change signal: r=0.14 after entropy control (weak)\n- Causal evidence: p=0.042 (barely significant)\n\n## Your Task\n\nWrite a detailed review covering:\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Novelty Assessment** (is each contribution genuinely new? is the combination sufficient?)\n3. **Related Work Gaps** (missing citations, positioning issues)\n4. **Framing and Writing Quality** (is the story coherent? are claims calibrated to evidence?)\n5. **Strengths** (bulleted)\n6. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, with severity)\n7. **Questions for Authors** (3-5)\n8. **Scores**: Soundness (1-4), Contribution (1-4), Clarity (1-4), Overall (1-6), Confidence (1-5)\n\nKey novelty questions to consider:\n- Is \"episode-level reward attribution\" genuinely novel, or is it just a standard REINFORCE-style approach that has been known for decades?\n- The credit assignment decay analysis (γ^(T-h)) is mathematically obvious once stated. Is characterizing it empirically sufficient contribution?\n- B-IAVR results are weak. Does the paper try to package a negative result as positive?\n- Self-Guide already achieves 72.7% on ALFWorld with Qwen-1.7B. This paper's episode-level training achieves 34.9%. How should this gap be interpreted?\n- Only 10 references. Is this sufficient for a venue paper?\n\nBe rigorous. Focus on whether the novelty bar is met for a top ML venue.\n","agentId":"ae19fc4ca933e3405","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review submitted. Here is a summary of the R2 assessment:\n\n**Overall: 3/6 (Weak Reject)**\n\nKey findings:\n\n1. **Episode-level GRPO has low novelty.** It is functionally equivalent to REINFORCE (1992) with trajectory returns. The gamma^(T-h) \"discovery\" is a mathematical tautology. The paper frames a one-line configuration fix as a methodological contribution.\n\n2. **B-IAVR results are marginal.** Actual improvements over confidence-threshold are +0.8pp (within seed noise). Even the dream paper's +2.5pp is not statistically distinguishable from zero given std=2.9pp.\n\n3. **Related work is critically inadequate.** 10 references in 3 paragraphs. Missing entire categories: classic RL credit assignment (GAE, RUDDER), concurrent agent RL (GiGPO at 86.1%, HCAPO, PA-MoE at 93.8%), selective verification competitors (Derailer-Rerailer, Agent-Omit, Sherlock), and the self-correction literature.\n\n4. **Absolute performance far below SOTA.** The paper achieves 34.9-48.2% on ALFWorld while Self-Guide gets 72.7% (same model) and PA-MoE+GiGPO gets 93.8% (smaller model). The \"8x improvement\" framing compares against a known-broken baseline, which is circular.\n\n5. **False dichotomy in credit assignment.** The paper presents only step-independent vs. episode-level, ignoring the rich intermediate spectrum (GiGPO nested groups, GAE, hindsight credit) that achieves higher performance.\n\nThe review was saved to `/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T235255/best/review_report.md`."}],"totalDurationMs":134731,"totalTokens":56335,"totalToolUseCount":15,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3675,"cache_read_input_tokens":52189,"output_tokens":470,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3675},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":470,"cache_read_input_tokens":52189,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3675,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3675,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":3,"searchCount":4,"bashCount":0,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":8}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UESPaVD3vU4Ss6gF5rYdQV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good, I have both reviews. Now I need to conduct the full roundtable:\n- Step 1: Independent reviews (done)\n- Step 2: Cross-share findings\n- Step 3: Converge on key points\n- Step 4: Synthesize final report\n\nLet me synthesize the reviews and conduct the roundtable discussion myself, then submit the final report.\n\nLet me compile the full reviews from both agents and then do the roundtable synthesis.\n\nR1 gave: 4/6 (Weak Accept) - focused on methods/experiments. Key issues: conflation of context window with credit assignment, no GiGPO comparison, absolute performance below SOTA, B-IAVR incremental.\n\n\nR2 gave: 3/6 (Weak Reject) - focused on novelty/related work. Key issues: episode-level GRPO is just REINFORCE, low novelty, inadequate related work (10 refs), absolute performance far below SOTA, B-IAVR marginal, false dichotomy.\n\nNow I'm converging their perspectives. Both reviewers agree on the performance gap relative to SOTA and the marginal contribution of B-IAVR, though they emphasize different aspects—R1 critiques the experimental design while R2 questions the fundamental novelty. I'll synthesize these into a consolidated assessment that captures the core weaknesses across both dimensions. I'm ready to rewrite the next thinking. Please provide it and I'll compress it to 1-3 sentences of natural prose, maintaining the first-person inner monologue style while avoiding any repetition of what's already been covered.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3603,"cache_read_input_tokens":57951,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3603},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"pa